Title: "Equivalent"
Id: "6bd988dd-59a8-4356-94cd-5bb2166c856f"

Text: "`Equivalent:` names an equivalence class whose `to:` entries are asserted to be
interchangeable with one another. Its `[...]` command heading names the class;
each `to:` command must use the header parameters exactly.

```mlg-fragment
[CommandHeader]
Equivalent:
using?: <DeclarationStatement>+
when?: <ClauseUnion>+
to: <Expression>+
Documented?: <DocumentedItemUnion>+
Justification?: <HaveGroup>+
References?: <ResourceHeader>+
Id?: <OpenText>
```

The `[CommandHeader]` heading is required and the `to:` section is required.
Unlike the definition-like groups, `Equivalent:` has no `Requires:`, `Enables:`,
`Aliases:`, `Writing:`, or `Metadata:` sections.

Each `to:` command must use the header parameters directly, as bare names — no
compound expressions and no `using:` symbols. The item is validated locally:

- every `to:` member must be defined and be a `Defines`, `Declares`, `States`,
  or `Refines` — and all members must be the same one of those kinds;
- the members must declare the same target shape, and (by kind) the same `is`
  type (`Defines`), the same declared `extends:` target (`Declares`), or the same base
  type (`Refines`);
- the members must provide the same set of capabilities, by name and arity; and
- this item's own `when:` must guarantee each member's requirements.

The members are then mutually substitutable to the type checker: a value known
to be one member (or the class-naming header) satisfies a requirement that it be
any other member, as long as the target member's header parameters are all
pinned to matching actuals by the known member. A capability or spec operator
the class provides likewise resolves on a value typed as any member or the
header.

```mlg-fragment
[\foo:of{a}:with{b}]
Equivalent:
using:
. n is \integer
when:
. a is \real
. b is \real
to:
. \bar{a, b}
. \baz:with{b}:and{a}
References:
. $book.foo
Id: \"11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111\"
```

The `Equivalent:` head is a marker and accepts no argument. Put reader-facing
names or explanation under `Documented:`."
Id: "543b077a-ba1e-4629-b04e-ca495754a218"
